<p><a name="fn5"></a> 5. Bank for International Settlements, Committee on Payment and Settlement Systems, <a href="https://www.bis.org/cpmi/publ/d52.pdf"><em>Policy Issues for Central Banks in Retail Payments</em> (PDF)</a> (Basel: BIS, March 2003). In some countries—such as Australia, the Netherlands, and Singapore—the central bank oversees all retail payment systems, whereas in others—such as Canada, Switzerland, and the United Kingdom—the central bank oversees systemically important payments, while another authority oversees payments that are not systemically important. <a href="#f5">Return to text</a></p>

<p><a name="fn6"></a>6. World Bank Group, <a href="http://pubdocs.worldbank.org/en/591241545960780368/GPSS-4-Report-Final.pdf"><em>Payment Systems Worldwide: A Snapshot</em> (PDF)</a> (Washington: World Bank, September 2018). <a href="#f6">Return to text</a></p>

