<p><a name="fn12"></a> 12. Cordruta Boar, Henry Holden, and Amber Wadsworth, <a href="https://www.bis.org/publ/bppdf/bispap107.htm"><em>Impending Arrival—A Sequel to the Survey on Central Bank Digital Currency</em></a> (Basel: Bank for International Settlements, January 2020). <a href="#f12">Return to text</a></p>

<p><a name="fn13"></a> 13. See Yuan Yang and Hudson Lockett, "What is China's Digital Currency Plan?" <em>Financial Times</em>, November 25, 2019, https://www.ft.com/content/e3f9c3c2-0aaf-11ea-bb52-34c8d9dc6d84; and Scott Horsley, <a href="https://www.npr.org/2020/01/13/795988512/ china-to-test-digital-currency-could-it-end-up-challenging-the-dollar-globally">"China to Test Digital Currency. Could It End up Challenging the Dollar Globally?"</a> National Public Radio, January 13, 2020. <a href="#f13">Return to text</a></p>

<p><a name="fn14"></a> 14. Michael Kumhof and Clare Noone, <a href="https://www.bankofengland.co.uk/-/media/boe/files/working-paper/2018/central-bank-digital-currencies-design-principles-and-balance-sheet-implications">"Central Bank Digital Currencies—Design Principles and Balance Sheet Implications,"</a> Bank of England Staff Working Paper no. 725 (London: Bank of England, May 2018). <a href="#f14">Return to text</a></p>
                     
